  "flags": {
    "mgt2": {
      "demo": {
        "order": 4,
        "cliff": "three graphs of ids, and none of them stores a name",
        "teaches": [
          "crew[].role holds the id of a role Item embedded on THIS ship. The code then finds a station by the derived crewRoleKey — never by the role's name.",
          "mounts[].weapons holds ids of weapon Items embedded on this same ship. A mount is not packaging: it decides the damage multiple.",
          "computer.running is a Set of ids of the programs that are STARTED. A program aboard but not in that Set spends no bandwidth and does nothing.",
          "hull.options and power.offline are Sets of closed, non-blank strings, and hull.pointsOverride is how a yard's printed Hull figure is stated without touching the derivation.",
          "fuel.tons is the design tank and ops.fuel the level actually aboard; neither derives from the other."
        ],
        "trap": "characteristics.hull.base stays 0. Hull points are DERIVED from hull.tons, hull.configuration and hull.options, and a base written here silently ADDS to them — the opposite of a vehicle, where hull.base is the printed figure. Two more to watch: crew[].dutyTarget is matched by the mount's LABEL or its 1-based index rather than by an id, and a spacecraft does NOT override the trait family, so a ship weapon's traits must say shipWeapon in as many words."
      }
    }
  },
